  "usage_note": "**Obviously** tells the listener that you think the fact is clear. Used to answer a question (*\"Obviously!\"*), it can sound rude, because it suggests that the question was silly. **Clearly** is a little more formal; **of course** is often the more polite choice in a reply.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Obviously that he is right.",
      "correct": "Obviously he is right.",
      "note": "No **that** follows **obviously**; say **It is obvious that he is right**, or use **obviously** alone."
    }
  ],
